  "decision_summary": "Predicted high (F >= 20%) because the most transferable evidence, perindopril (structurally related ACE-inhibitor ester prodrug), shows absolute oral bioavailability of 66–95% in fasted subjects and 30 ± 6% in cirrhotic patients, both above threshold; L4 intestinal absorption/permeability/solubility records are for other molecules and provide no affirmative evidence of F < 20% for the query."
}

